From: kofec
Subject: [PATCH] drm/probe-helper: match the interlace flag of a video= mode

drm_helper_probe_add_cmdline_mode() marks the first probed mode with the
size and refresh of video= as USERDEF, whether interlaced or not. With
video=HDMI-A-1:1920x1080@50 the WeTek Play on a projector whose EDID lists
1080i50 (VIC 20) before 1080p50 (VIC 31) came up in 1080i50, although
the command line has no "i": drm_connector_pick_cmdline_mode() returns a
USERDEF mode before its own interlace-aware search. The Meson6 OSD does
not handle an interlaced output (the GUI came out stretched and cut off),
and 50 Hz progressive was the point.

Skip probed modes whose interlace flag differs from the command line.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c
@@ -163,6 +163,15 @@
 				continue;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * 1920x1080i50 and 1920x1080p50 share size and refresh: without
+		 * an "i" in video= only a progressive mode may match, or the
+		 * first one in EDID order wins (an interlaced one on many sinks).
+		 */
+		if (!!(mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE) !=
+		    cmdline_mode->interlace)
+			continue;
+
 		/* Mark the matching mode as being preferred by the user */
 		mode->type |= DRM_MODE_TYPE_USERDEF;
 		return 0;
